// Stand-in dimensions of the scout 4x4 for pictures and tests, PROVISIONAL(C-002) until the skin is built from FORGE's VehicleDef
// (`skin::Skin::from_def`). They are the numbers of content/vehicles/game/scout_4x4.ron, and a test checks that they still agree: hull box
// 3.7 x 1.65 x 1.55 m (above the underside, which is 0.30 m off the ground), axles 0.65 m and 2.85 m from the front, track 1.35 m, tyre 0.70 m
// across by 0.20 m. The rim and the lugs are the stand-in wheel's proportions (placeholder_wheel.ron) at this radius (0.35 / 0.40), as `Skin::from_def` makes them. Provenance ESTIMATE, band +-5% each.
SkinSpec(
    dims: (
        length_m: 3.7,
        width_m: 1.65,
        height_m: 1.55,
        wheelbase_m: 2.2,
        track_m: 1.35,
        ground_clearance_m: 0.30,
        wheel: (outer_radius_m: 0.35, width_m: 0.20, rim_radius_m: 0.21, lug_depth_m: 0.0175, lugs_around: 25),
    ),
    axles_from_front_m: [0.65, 2.85],
    steered: [true, false],
)
